{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Amend the Patient Safety Commissioner\u2019s remit to cover all NHS-funded healthcare",
        "additional_details": "Patient safety concerns can arise from diagnosis, treatment, communication, clinical records and continuity of care, and can involve several NHS services or organisations.\r\n\r\nThe Patient Safety Commissioner\u2019s statutory remit is currently focused on medicines and medical devices. We believe patients should have an independent national commissioner able to identify systemic safety concerns across NHS-funded healthcare and ensure patients\u2019 experiences inform improvements in safety.",
        "background": "Amend the Medicines and Medical Devices Act 2021 so that the Patient Safety Commissioner\u2019s core duties extend beyond medicines and medical devices to promoting patient safety across all NHS-funded healthcare in England.",
